WEBVTT

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.240
Hop, step, jump.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.140
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.950
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.400
Who I wanna be. 

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.650
They call me calm, strong, and cool. 

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.000
Everyone says I'm popular.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.410
But the truth is, I'm not like that at all. 

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.620
I'm just an ordinary girl! 

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.730
I wish I could just get rid 

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:54.510
of all this pressure and be myself. 

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.350
But they'd all say it's out of character. 

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.760
Unlock my heart! 

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:08.110
Just be who you wanna be. 

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.960
Your Guardian Characters are with you. 

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.210
Just do it the way you wanna do it. 

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.280
It'll be okay, really! 

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.190
Just be who you wanna be. 

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.960
Having only one style would be way too boring. 

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.220
Just do it the way you wanna do it. 

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:34.490
You can do anything! 

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:36.110
I know that...

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.950
Hop, step, jump.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.840
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.710
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.020
...is who I wanna be. 

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.740
Next.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:01:59.930
Thanks.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:06.470
So anyway...

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.570
Did you see today's Good Morning TV?

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:09.520
Yeah, I saw it!

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.100
Na-chin's dad had a lot of screen time!

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.810
What? On TV? Really? Why?

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:19.080
He'll be performing a traditional Japanese dance at a national theater soon.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.020
Nadeshiko's father is the head of the Fujisaki School, which teaches the Kazeyanagi style.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:23.810
That's right.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.450
Japanese arts?

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.430
Fujisaki School.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.000
Japanese arts.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.810
Fujisaki School.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:34.390
Japanese Martial Arts

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.530
Master!

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:34.390
Right.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:40.370
Fujisaki Wave!

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:43.770
Wrong.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.280
You've got it wrong.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.660
Fujisaki Wave       Japanese Martial Arts

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.270
Fujisaki School        Japanese Traditional Dance

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.440
"Nichibu" is traditional Japanese dance.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.400
It's a tradition at the very heart and soul of Japan.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.380
I knew that. I just spaced out for a second!

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:03.690
I guess you don't know that Na-chin's family runs a famous dance school, did you?

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:04.460
No.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:10.060
They're amazingly Japanese. You could almost call them the Fujisaki Clan!

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.390
Fujisaki Clan

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.070
Freaky!

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.390
No, no, we're quite normal.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:42.000
I act like I'm her friend, but I suppose I don't know all that much about Nadeshiko's family.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:48.810
Bye!

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:49.890
Talk to you later!

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.720
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.180
Amu-chan.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:58.820
Still a scaredy-cat, I see.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.180
W-What do you mean?

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.890
Are you free tomorrow?

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.390
If you'd like, you should come hang out at my place.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:09.870
And since tomorrow's Saturday, you could even stay the night.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.970
The Seven Mysteries of the Fujisaki Family!?

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.970
Episode 9

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.470
Whitey Whitey

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.470
W-What is this?

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:24.820
Take this with you to Nadeshiko's tomorrow.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.390
But why detergent?

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.520
Because it's the most highly-prized gift a married woman could hope to receive!

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:31.910
Housewife's Wisdom Monthly
2007 Year-end Gift Survey
Things They'd Love to Get!!

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.970
In the survey my magazine did, towels came in at a close second, but inevitably lost.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.900
Nadeshiko's mom isn't like that!

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.910
She's an instructor of the Fujisaki School's Kazeyanagi style.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.600
Fujisaki School?

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:48.160
Fujisaki Wave!

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:51.060
Not like that. I made the same mistake.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:55.900
You know, it's pretty rare for you to sleep over at a friend's house.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.760
Now that you mention it...

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.000
I-It's not that rare.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.690
Never mind, I'm going to bed.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:05.020
Ready, and...

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.810
Got it!

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:16.450
If you ask me, you're taking way too much stuff for one night.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.430
Found it!

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:21.300
You want to add more?

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.640
Fortune-telling cards!

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.840
I'm going to stay at a friend's house.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.770
I've never done that before.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:32.730
Hey, let's invite Amu-chan to our next sleepover.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:36.270
Okay, but I don't think she's into that sort of thing.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.390
Yeah, that's true.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:41.980
We're beat.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.210
Amu-chan, I'm coming in.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:50.610
My goodness. If you pack all that, you won't have room for the detergent.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.750
I'm not taking it.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.470
You know...

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.570
I'm going with you!

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:03.630
Ami-chan, don't say that.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.960
I'm going! I'm going! I'm going! I'm going!

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.980
All right! Ami-chan can come with me to the park!

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:10.800
We'll take lots of pictures!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:11.680
Don't wanna go with Daddy!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.390
"Don't wanna?!"

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:16.950
I wanna go with you, Sis!

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.180
I guess it's true. Your daddy is... Your daddy is...

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:17.940
Good grief.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.360
There are ghosts.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.410
My friend's house is full of ghosts.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.600
They call them...

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:32.060
The Seven Wonders of the Fujisaki Family.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:34.560
The walking Japanese doll.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.020
The Noh-masked murderer!

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.220
The gigantic, poisonous centipede!

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:41.220
The living suit of armor!

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:43.180
The creature that treads above the ceiling!

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:45.640
The dragon that leaps out of a hanging scroll!

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:52.470
Amu-chan, Amu-chan, you only listed six.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:57.440
Anyway! Like I said, I'm going to my friend's house to get rid of ghosts.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.870
Ghosts are super scary.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.970
Isn't that exactly what Madame Saeki Nobuko said?

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:04.470
Those who call them stupid will die!

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.610
But if you still want to come...

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:09.020
Sis, come back alive!

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:11.700
I'm off.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.680
Be careful, okay?

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:18.180
She said it'd be obvious once I got close, but...

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.160
This is huge!

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:23.850
That's one enormous mansion.

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:29.640
It's big all right, and I can somehow believe it might actually have ghosts.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.950
I'll just ring the doorbe-

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:36.090
Wai-

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:48.130
Oh dear. Forgive me. I thought that pesky salesman was back again.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:51.850
Baya? Oh, Amu-chan.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:52.890
Welcome.

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:59.440
Oh, this is Baya-san. She looks after the house for us.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.180
Nice to meet you!

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:05.540
Baya-san? I've never met a real nanny bef- 

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.640
She's so astonished by everything.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:13.370
Nadeshiko really is a high-class girl.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:24.140
Wow, her mom is so beautiful.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.060
It would be proper etiquette to have the head of the house entertain you.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:35.380
Unfortunately, he is currently away preparing for his performance. Please accept my apology.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:38.390
I-It is no problem at all.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:39.890
Enjoy your tea.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.350
She's spinning it way too fast.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:53.890
Hinamori-san.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.020
Yes?!

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.030
What is that?

00:08:57.150 --> 00:08:58.350
This?

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.930
It that, perhaps, detergent?

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:03.640
This will help immensely!

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:04.390
Baya.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:07.170
My word! Rated number one in cleansing power,

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:10.220
leaving the delicate fragrance of whiteness: Whitey Whitey! 

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:12.090
Please give your mother our thanks.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:13.180
Yeah, sure.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:16.740
I guess we were fooled by her outer character.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.750
Amu-chan, would you like to watch my dance practice?

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.640
Oh, yes.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:42.850
Nadeshiko's so pretty. If I was a guy, I think I'd fall in love with her in a heartbeat.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.170
Would you like to give it a try?

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:50.010
What a splendid idea.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:52.850
Baya, would you prepare a kimono?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:58.520
Actually, I suspected you might make such a request, so here you are.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.060
You always know just what to do.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:01.680
Uh, um...

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:03.130
Now...

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:04.260
Now...

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:05.620
Now...

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:10.960
Is that really me?

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.380
Lovely, don't you think?

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.010
Yeah.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:17.430
I mean, I was talking about the kimono, not me, and...

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.880
She dances so beautifully.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:52.390
Though her form is not quite right, there's something about those who have radiant hearts.

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:55.490
Why don't you scout her while you can?

00:10:57.170 --> 00:11:01.270
I wonder why my heart is racing and I feel so happy.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.810
Amu-chan, you're awesome.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.270
You're not so bad.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:09.680
You're cute!

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.120
My foot cramped!

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.360
Amu-chan, calm down.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.270
Wh-What was that about scouting?

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:22.600
It kind of went down the drain.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:40.020
The Fujisaki Family has a long history of running a Japanese dance school.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:43.600
This house itself was built over one hundred years ago.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.220
Doesn't that just make it old?

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:51.900
You jest, but if we simply perform the necessary repairs...

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:56.090
Good evening, Mr. Mouse.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:58.600
Temari-chan?

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:04.480
You dirty rat! How dare you sully the name of the Fujisaki Family in the presence of guests!

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:09.810
Bother, he escaped.

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:11.930
U-Uh...

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:15.260
Failure! Will you scoundrels go to war with me or not?!

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:17.180
Yes, Sir!

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:20.720
Something is about to happen to you. 

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.590
You'll have to be careful.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.890
One more time.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:27.750
Nadeshiko-san.

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:28.600
Yes?

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:35.970
It's already past eleven, please take a bath soon.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.380
Which means...

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:40.950
Huh? That means four hours have already gone by.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.700
Amu-chan, would you like to go first?

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:43.520
Oh, sure.

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:46.810
This way.

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:48.080
Okay!

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:05.640
The bath was huge, too! I could've been at a hot spring!

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:08.640
Huh?

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:19.890
Am I... Am I lost?

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:31.360
What... What is this sound?

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.720
The walking Japanese doll?

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:37.950
No way! Not a chance!

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:53.680
Did you hear Amu-chan's voice just now?

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:57.220
Idiot! That rat'll catch on to us.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.850
Darn it! We're moving to the next plan!

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:04.960
Why are we even helping you exterminate rats in the first place?

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:07.100
We're supposed to be guests, too.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.770
Please allow us to help you!

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.760
It's true! I saw it move!

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:14.470
That's not possible.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:16.640
Those who call them stupid will die!

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:20.010
Oh, my mother did tell me...

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.070
But don't worry.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:26.520
I <i>am</i> worried! Who wouldn't be after you just stop like that?!

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:33.310
Legend says that a long time ago, before this house was built, a demon lived in this area.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:35.060
A demon?!

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:39.250
It masqueraded as a kind, elderly woman, who'd invite travelers to stay the night.

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:41.890
But once they fell asleep, the demon would have its way with them.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:44.600
We should sleep.

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:46.100
Who could sleep after that?!

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:54.890
I wonder where Ran and everyone else is. They're never around when I need them.

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:58.220
Na-Nadeshiko, are you awake?

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:00.020
I am.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.950
Don't fall asleep before me, okay?

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:05.220
Oh, not that I'm scared of ghosts or anything.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:07.720
I'm in the fifth grade now. I'm not a kid anymore, you know.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:12.470
I just don't want such a fun day to end so soon. And you know, I'm not all that tired.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:15.140
Plus, it's hard to sleep on an unfamiliar pillow.

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:17.490
Wake up!

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.310
Why are you playing with the breaker?!

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.140
He ran away.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.640
Boss, we chasin' him?

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:33.840
Darn right we are!

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.640
Yes, Sir!

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:39.310
What's that?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:44.810
Don't tell me... The creature that walks above the ceiling?!

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:53.750
God! Buddha! Or even Saeki Nobuko!

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:57.860
If a ghost appears, you must <i>not</i> look away, no matter what.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:02.770
If it sees that you are feint of heart, you will die!

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:05.480
Yeah, that's right, I can't look away.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.560
If I look away...

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.580
The gigantic, poisonous centipede?!

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:14.720
T-Too heavy.

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:16.400
I can't go on.

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:20.220
Put your backs into it! Show me what you Guardian Characters are made of!

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.950
You meddlesome rat!

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:28.520
Um, Boss?

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:29.470
What?!

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:31.970
We can fly.

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:49.220
What is going on here?

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:53.800
If you keep doing as you please, you'll cause problems for the rest of us.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:06.790
Nadeshiko-san.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.190
Sorry, Amu-chan.

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:26.220
This pattern can only mean...

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:36.240
Shh! What'll you do if we're discovered?!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.830
What do you mean, discovered?

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.140
I mean it, be quiet!

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:45.170
The truth is, we've all been tricked. This isn't Nadeshiko's house at all.

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.300
Nadeshiko and her mom are both fakes!

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:53.420
It's a demonic mansion that takes in travelers and kills them! It's been resurrected!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.660
There's no way that's true.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:18:00.940
Let's go. It's time for the House of Horrors Escape Plan. All loud noises are off-limits, okay?

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:02.350
Yes, Sir.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.880
I can't be caught doing this.

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:13.470
Good night.

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:18.600
This is bad. I have no idea where I am.

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:22.220
What's that?

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:31.550
Nadeshiko-san, how many times must I repeat myself?

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:33.840
You're sliding your feet too aggressively!

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.720
I'm sorry, Mother.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.220
We should stop for tonight.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.430
No!

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.310
Please watch me a little longer.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.310
I won't make it in time for the performance!

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:46.310
I understand.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:50.210
She's trying to make up her lost practice time.

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:53.350
She even left quietly so Amu-chan wouldn't notice.

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:55.780
How sweet of her.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:19:01.220
I knew all along that her traditional dance performance was coming up, but I still came to hang out.

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:04.470
Nadeshiko was even considerate enough to invite me.

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:09.810
And I got so caught up in the excitement, I didn't once think about how Nadeshiko would be affected.

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:13.510
I might kind of fail as a friend.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:15.970
That's absolutely not true.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:22.430
Nothing is more precious to Nadeshiko-sama than Japanese dance.

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:28.180
That's why when she suggested inviting you here...

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:32.470
You do understand, correct? This is a critical period.

00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:35.850
You've no time to fritter about with a friend.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:39.120
I'm aware of that, Mother.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.220
Then you can choose another day, and...

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.140
No!

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:50.270
That was the first time I've ever seen Nadeshiko-sama choose a friend over practice.

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:53.220
I was quite stunned.

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:54.890
But...

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:57.720
I understand.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.720
Mother.

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:03.290
The expression on your face is quite lovely, Nadeshiko-san.

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:07.230
She must be one important friend.

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:08.390
She is.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:11.520
Look at that.

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:15.210
Nadeshiko-sama's mother is currently instructing with great stringency.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:19.480
But this is the first time I've seen Nadeshiko have such exquisite form.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:24.020
Those with radiant hearts always shine, no matter what they do.

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:30.640
Hinamori-san, you're the one making Nadeshiko's heart shine.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:31.770
I am?

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:37.640
Please continue to be her friend.

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:45.220
Sorry for all the trouble.

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:47.670
Have a safe trip home.

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:48.390
I will.

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:53.220
I didn't get much sleep last night.

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:00.400
Nothing. Thanks for everything.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:09.640
Hey, Nadeshiko, I'm really glad my first sleepover was at your house.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.100
Thanks, Nadeshiko.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:21.650
I'm back.

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:23.520
Welcome back!

00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:26.640
Sis, did you get the ghosts?

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:29.210
Indeed. I have sealed them all.

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:30.980
They were all worthy opponents.

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:33.630
Way cool, Sis! Way cool!

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:37.170
Amu-chan, did you give them the detergent?

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:38.520
Yeah, I did.

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:40.970
Here. This is from Nadeshiko's mom.

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:43.970
T-This is...

00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:47.970
The second most sought-after gift: a towel set!

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:50.210
You're good, Nadeshiko-chan's mother.

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:52.100
I underestimated you because you're a celebrity.

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:55.120
Amu-chan, when are you planning to go over there again?!

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.270
W-We don't have anything scheduled.

00:21:57.270 --> 00:22:03.690
I see. I should take this opportunity to do a new survey.

00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:07.680
But I would like to go again sometime.

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:40.790
As long as I exist, even when I'm a pile of dust, 

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:47.190
I'll keep cheering "you can do it, you can do it" out loud! 

00:22:47.190 --> 00:22:48.010
(You can do it!)

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:54.170
I'll never stop as long as I live,  

00:22:54.170 --> 00:23:00.520
so I'll sing my never-ending song. 

00:23:01.420 --> 00:23:05.030
I'll press forward down my path. 

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:08.550
Even random characters have their merits. 

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:13.390
You might be worthless, but I'll still love you, 

00:23:13.390 --> 00:23:14.860
my darling.

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:18.650
You idiot! My true self... 

00:23:18.650 --> 00:23:21.610
Just say what's on your mind. 

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:25.040
You're sticking out a little. 

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:28.310
You're coming closer to my dream. 

00:23:28.310 --> 00:23:32.090
You jerk! My true self... 

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:36.340
Please come out, don't hide. 

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:41.280
Oh yeah! Right now! 

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:53.720
Everyone! Please listen to my troubles!

00:23:53.720 --> 00:23:55.680
Move out of the way for a second, Su.

00:23:55.680 --> 00:23:58.070
Character Transformation: Amulet Heart!

00:23:58.070 --> 00:24:01.650
Let me try again. Please listen to my-

00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:03.220
Su, move it!

00:24:03.220 --> 00:24:05.850
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:09.810
Su wants to Character Transform, too!

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:11.090
Next time on Shugo Chara:

00:24:11.090 --> 00:24:13.010
Character Transformation! Amulet Clover!

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:14.150
That title...

00:24:14.150 --> 00:24:15.470
Kind of spills the beans.

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:17.910
Watch it, pretty please!
